 "evidence_class": "SELF_MEASURED_DIRTY",
 "finding": "Combined verdict MIXED (MLP MIXED, DeltaNet MIXED). MLP production 329.6 GB/s, ARM A (stripped) 497.4 GB/s (1.5089x), ARM B (half K) time/byte 1.0427 (time_ratio 0.5214, byte_ratio 0.5). DeltaNet qkvz production 600.9 GB/s, ARM A 943.2 GB/s (1.5697x), ARM B time/byte 1.1022. Pre-registered rule: MIXED. ARM A jumped but ARM B tracked bytes (half K also halves FMAs, so linear scaling is predicted by both ALU and bandwidth); the pre-registered rule will not promote that pair to ALU_BOUND. ARM A landing near the LM-head rate with surviving loads is evidence that production arithmetic is expensive, but ARM B halves K (and therefore also halves FMAs), so linear time/byte is predicted by both ALU and bandwidth and cannot close the conjunction. Do not promote to ALU_BOUND. Do not rescue a refuted layout lever with this result.",
